  "question": {
    "text": "Let a triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> be inscribed in the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. If the length of side&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>,&nbsp;then the area of the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#9651;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to:"
  },
